# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore, so this file applies ONLY to
# apps/docs/Dockerfile and leaves the other five images alone.
#
# Without it this image did not merely build slowly, it did not build at all: the context is
# the repo root, so `COPY . .` dragged the host's node_modules into the deps layer, and
# `pnpm install` then aborted with ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY rather than
# purge a modules directory it could not ask about. The context was also 1.7GB.
#
# The fix is to not copy any of it. Setting CI=true would only silence the prompt while
# still shipping 1.7GB into a build layer.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
**/build
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/.astro
**/.source
.git

# Credentials have no business in a build layer, even a discarded one.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
deploy/certs

# Visual regression screenshots and local planning notes: the build uses neither.
apps/web/baseline
apps/web/after
.superpowers

**/npm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store
